{"causes": ["The intellectual ferment of 12th and 13th-century Marrakesh fostered a climate conducive to historical scholarship.", "The profound socio-political transformations brought about by the Almohad Caliphate created an urgent need for comprehensive historical documentation.", "Al-Marrākushī's access to both contemporary written records and living witnesses provided him with invaluable primary source material."], "effects": ["His *Kitāb al-muʿjib* became an indispensable primary source for all subsequent historians studying the Almohad Caliphate and medieval North Africa.", "The work preserved detailed accounts of Almohad religious doctrine, political administration, and military campaigns that would otherwise be lost.", "It offered a near-contemporary, critical perspective on the Almohad dynasty, influencing how later scholars understood its rise and decline."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "almohad-caliphate", "sourceName": "Almohad Caliphate", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "abd-al-wahid-al-marrakushi", "targetName": "ʻAbd al-Wāḥid al-Marrākushī", "context": "The political and cultural dominance of the Almohad Caliphate provided the primary subject matter and context for al-Marrākushī's historical work."}, {"sourceSlug": "abd-al-wahid-al-marrakushi", "sourceName": "ʻAbd al-Wāḥid al-Marrākushī", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "marrakesh", "targetName": "Marrakesh", "context": "ʻAbd al-Wāḥid al-Marrākushī lived and likely composed significant parts of his historical chronicle in Marrakesh, the Almohad capital."}, {"sourceSlug": "abd-al-wahid-al-marrakushi", "sourceName": "ʻAbd al-Wāḥid al-Marrākushī", "verb": "CREATES", "targetSlug": "kitab-al-mujib-fi-talkhis-akhbar-al-maghrib", "targetName": "Kitāb al-muʿjib fī talkhīṣ akhbār al-Maghrib", "context": "ʻAbd al-Wāḥid al-Marrākushī authored the seminal historical chronicle *Kitāb al-muʿjib fī talkhīṣ akhbār al-Maghrib* around 1224 CE."}, {"sourceSlug": "kitab-al-mujib-fi-talkhis-akhbar-al-maghrib", "sourceName": "Kitāb al-muʿjib fī talkhīṣ akhbār al-Maghrib", "verb": "TRANSMITS", "targetSlug": "almohad-history", "targetName": "Almohad History", "context": "Al-Marrākushī's *Kitāb al-muʿjib* served as a critical vehicle for transmitting detailed historical knowledge about the Almohad Caliphate to later generations."}, {"sourceSlug": "abd-al-wahid-al-marrakushi", "sourceName": "ʻAbd al-Wāḥid al-Marrākushī", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "ibn-khaldun", "targetName": "Ibn Khaldūn", "context": "Al-Marrākushī's historical methodology and detailed accounts likely influenced later Maghrebi historians, including the renowned Ibn Khaldūn."}], "places": [{"name": "Marrakesh, Morocco", "role": "Birthplace and intellectual center"}, {"name": "Fez, Morocco", "role": "Center of learning"}, {"name": "Al-Andalus", "role": "Geographic scope of historical work"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: ʻAbd al-Wāḥid al-Marrākushī", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "ʻabd-al-wāḥid-al-marrākushī"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4664888", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abd_al-Wahid_al-Marrakushi"], "tags": ["Journalists & Chroniclers", "cause-and-effect", "cultural-diffusion", "temporal-linkage"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "ʻAbd al-Wāḥid al-Marrākushī's *Kitāb al-muʿjib* is a foundational primary source, indispensable for understanding the Almohad Caliphate and 12th-13th century North African history, directly shaping subsequent scholarship for centuries.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-09-02T23:14:45Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#33693998490", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Abd al-Wahid al-Marrakushi was a Maghrebi historian who lived during the Almohad period.", "newValue": "ʻAbd al-Wāḥid al-Marrākushī, a pivotal 13th-century Maghrebi historian, flourished during the twilight of the Almohad Caliphate, providing an indispensable, near-contemporary account of one of North Africa's most significant imperial periods. Born in Marrakesh around 1185 CE and dying circa 1300 CE, his magnum opus, *Kitāb al-muʿjib fī talkhīṣ akhbār al-Maghrib* (The Amazing Book in Summarizing the History of the Maghreb), stands as a cornerstone for understanding the political, social, and cultural landscape of the Maghreb and al-Andalus from the Almoravid ascendancy through the Almohad decline.

His *Kitāb al-muʿjib*, completed around 1224 CE, meticulously chronicles the rise and fall of the Almohad dynasty, from its origins in the Masmuda Berber movement led by Ibn Tūmart to its eventual fragmentation. Al-Marrākushī's work is celebrated for its detailed narratives of key figures like Abd al-Mu'min and Abū Yūsuf Yaʿqūb al-Manṣūr, significant battles such as Alarcos (1195 CE), and the administrative and intellectual achievements of the Almohad era. His unique position allowed him to draw upon both written sources, some now lost, and oral testimonies from individuals who had lived through or directly participated in the events he describes, lending his history a rare immediacy and authenticity.

The enduring legacy of al-Marrākushī lies in his chronicle's status as a primary source, shaping nearly all subsequent historical narratives concerning the Almohads. Without *Kitāb al-muʿjib*, modern historians would possess a far less nuanced understanding of the Almohad Caliphate's ideological underpinnings, military campaigns, and intellectual flourishing, particularly its contributions to law, theology, and philosophy. His work served as a vital bridge, transmitting knowledge across generations and informing later chroniclers like Ibn Khaldūn, thereby securing its place as an essential text in Islamic historiography."}, {"timestamp": "2026-09-02T23:14:45Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#33693998490", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": [{"title": "Medieval era: interplay of religious authority, feudal governance, and trade network expansion", "type": "EventWindow", "year": "1185-07-07, Marrakesh"}, {"title": "Rise of print media and public discourse", "type": "Idea", "year": "1185-07-07, Marrakesh"}], "newValue": ["The intellectual ferment of 12th and 13th-century Marrakesh fostered a climate conducive to historical scholarship.", "The profound socio-political transformations brought about by the Almohad Caliphate created an urgent need for comprehensive historical documentation.", "Al-Marrākushī's access to both contemporary written records and living witnesses provided him with invaluable primary source material."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-09-02T23:14:45Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#33693998490", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": [{"title": "Shaped public opinion and historical record", "type": "Idea", "year": "1300"}, {"title": "Contributed to synthesis of classical and religious thought informing Renaissance and Reformati", "type": "Movement", "year": "1300"}], "newValue": ["His *Kitāb al-muʿjib* became an indispensable primary source for all subsequent historians studying the Almohad Caliphate and medieval North Africa.",